{"name":"Coast Cream","hex":"#f6e6db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coast","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The edge of the land where it meets an ocean, sea, gulf, bay, or large lake. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The side or edge of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To glide along without adding energy; to allow a vehicle to continue moving forward after disengaging the engine or ceasing to apply motive power.","To sail along a coast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coast"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast","wikidata":"Q93352"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rugged coastline of the West Coast Region of New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/500px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/1280px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/500px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Somalia has the longest coastline in Africa.[12]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASomalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg/500px-Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg/1280px-Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg/500px-Porto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Atlantic rocky coastline, showing a surf area. Porto Covo, west coast of Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APorto_Covo_pano_April_2009-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Spiaggia_rosa%2C_isola_di_budelli%2C_sardegna.jpg/500px-Spiaggia_rosa%2C_isola_di_budelli%2C_sardegna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_